    -binwidth on geom_histogram controls the size of the histograms bars (bigger the number= more bars and vice versa)
    -density plot is a smoothed out version of a histogram used for continuous data (contains less detail but is more plesant on the eye to see data)
    -position = "fill" in geom bar fills in the histograms blank areas, useful for comparing destribution of data
    -labs() forces a change in label
    -if data gets cluttered by too many aesthetic mappings, split the data into facets (subplots to display one subset of data) USE facet_wrap then ~ and add category
    -LABELS ARE IMPORTANT!! error: two legends representing same data, make sure lab of the data is upper/lowercase
